## Goal
Make `scripts/install.sh` treat a failed or timed-out `lsregister -u` (unregistering stale app copies) as an install failure instead of only a warning. This came out of a cross-review.

## Problems
None.

## Decision
- `unreg()` now records a non-zero status when the unregister command fails or the 10 s watchdog kills it. It prints an `error:` message instead of a `warning:` and returns that status.
- The sweep loop no longer reads from a pipe. A pipe runs the loop in a subshell, so a `sweep_failed=1` set inside it would be lost. The loop now reads `$others_list` through a here-document and runs in the main shell, so `unreg "$p" || sweep_failed=1` reaches the existing failure handling.
- The new app is still registered first, and the install fails only afterwards (exit 1). This leaves the system in a usable state while the failure is still reported.

